                                                             tagged 3181-3184
  stack port4.0.26 (member 4, 1000BASE-SX) -- SA port1.0.26  TRUNK: tagged 3181-3184 + 3189, native none
  SA port1.0.2 -- eth2 (tb470)                               access vlan 3189 (SA bridges only, no SVI)
  per VRRP VLAN i = 1..4 (vlan318i, VRID 8i):
    stack vlan318i 10.118.i.1/24, VRRP priority 200 | SA vlan318i 10.118.i.3/24, VRRP priority 100
    virtual IP 10.118.i.254 (not owned: `virtual-ip ... backup` on both)
    fake host 10.118.i.2, MAC 02:31:18:94:00:0i, gateway = virtual MAC 0000.5e00.015i
  destination: stack vlan3189 10.118.9.1/24; host 10.118.9.2 = static ARP to fake MAC
    0231.1894.0009 on port4.0.26; SA `mac address-table static 0231.1894.0009 forward
    interface port1.0.2 vlan 3189` (no flooding). eth2 counts in promiscuous mode (tb470 has
    ip_forward=1, so fake MACs keep the host out of the path; memory/T3116 method).
  Frames: tools/mkvrrp.py, round-robin across the four VLANs, UDP sport 5000+i -> 5001, so
    the receiver counts each VLAN separately (tools/18948-traffic.sh).
  The SX link's baseline access VLAN 4000, port3.0.10's access vlan 1 and SA port1.0.2's
  vlan 1 were changed for the case and restored after it.

